    <sys:String x:Key="Onboarding_Title">Welcome to HideEverything</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Onboarding_Intro">Use a global shortcut to remove app windows from the screen, taskbar, and Alt+Tab, then bring them back with the same shortcut. HideEverything stays in the system tray.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Onboarding_QuickStart">Quick start</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Onboarding_Step1">1.  Open Settings from the tray icon (double-click it, or right-click and choose Settings).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Onboarding_Step2">2.  Click “Add controlled app…” and choose a running app or browse for an exe file.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Onboarding_Step3">3.  New apps start with Alt+D; click Set… to change the shortcut.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Onboarding_Step4">4.  Press the shortcut to hide/show; multiple apps can share one shortcut.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Onboarding_Step5">5.  The tool's tray entry always remains available; configure its language and shortcuts in Settings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Onboarding_Warning">Note: exclusive full-screen apps may not hide reliably. Use borderless windowed mode. Press Ctrl+Alt+backtick at any time to restore all hidden windows.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Onboarding_OpenSettings">Open Settings</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Onboarding_Done">Got it</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="AddApp_Title">Add controlled app</sys:String>
